   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Old sentences, still in use",
     "texto": [
      "A **refrán** packs advice into one sentence. People often say only the beginning and let the other person finish it: «Ya sabes, no por mucho madrugar…»\n\nTheir grammar is old and compact, and you now have the tools to read it.\n\n- **No hay mal que por bien no venga**: a relative clause in the subjunctive after «no hay».\n- **No por mucho madrugar amanece más temprano**: «por mucho» + infinitive means «however much you do it».\n- **De tal palo, tal astilla**: there is no verb at all. From such a stick, such a splinter.\n- **A caballo regalado no le mires el diente**: a negative command.\n- **Más vale** X **que** Y: X is worth more than Y.\n- **Quien mucho abarca, poco aprieta**: whoever takes on a lot, holds little tight."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "How proverbs are built",
     "texto": [
      "Proverbs use compact forms.\n\n- **No verb**: **De tal palo, tal astilla**. The verb is understood: «de tal palo sale tal astilla».\n- **Command order**: **A caballo regalado no le mires el diente**. It speaks to anyone.\n- **Comparison with «más vale»**: **Más vale** pájaro en mano **que** ciento volando.\n- **Subject with «quien»**: **Quien** mucho abarca, poco aprieta. «Quien» equals «la persona que».\n- **Negative sentence with subjunctive**: **No hay mal que** por bien no **venga**.\n\nTo use them well, quote them whole or start one and let the other person finish."
     ],
